{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1518965-nagual-the-savage","id":1518965,"title":"Nagual: The Savage!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-27T15:31:06-07:00","id":1518965,"title":"Nagual: The Savage!","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:22px\">Nagual: The Ignited</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">A Storytelling Game of Duty and Community</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">A Fan-Splat by Tonkers77</span><br /> <br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1286_1690496974734_704\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1286\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1286\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1286&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/>\u200b</div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Nagual!</span></div> <br /> \u200b\u200bHello! Nagual the Ignited is a Fan-Splat created by myself for playing a Shapeshifter in the CofD. They are not of the Shadow in any way, so they can be played alongside the Uratha of Werewolf.<br /> <br /> Instead, they protect the material and maintain humanity through cultivating its relationship with the rest of Lurra's Creations. As far as they are concerned, Lurra-Ulaka is a the primal goddess of the cycle of life and death, predator and prey, and all living mundane things. This includes humanity. A divine spark of her power runs through their veins in the form of the Rage.<br /> <br /> Her Garden, the material world, is under attack. It is being invaded by a force called the Absence whose inhabitants, Invasives, crawl through the cracks between the Absence and the material to manifest and feed. They warp entire habitats and landscapes in order to better thrive. Consider them more of an Invasive Species than the crazy, evil of the Wyrm stuff.<br /> <br /> Nagual are born to the three Breeds, Glede the Nagual Born (They are not like the metis. No curse or twisting, not sterile, just raised among Nagual from the get-go); Scoria the Animal Born (No, Nagual do not get it on with animals. Only Lurra-Ulaka decides if an animal becomes Nagual) and finally the Kindled or Human Born. Humans who were Kindled by the Rage of another Nagual into undergoing the Call.<br /> <br /> Every Nagual is part of a Brood that share the same animal shape. These also cause them to pick up particular quirks of that animal as well. Raccoons will put their hands on your stuff, Cats like to watch things, and Wolves are super social.\u200b<br /> <br /> Nagual also Adapt to their surroundings, their Rage honing itself to make them the perfect predators of whatever they're dealing with, or are among. This gives them plenty of Crossover options, as immersing yourself into the business of other Splats opens up particular Supernatural Adaptations.<br /> <br /> Adaptations come in four flavors. Brood Adaptations can only be learned by the particular Brood, like the Grimalkin being the only ones that learn Adaptation of the Cat. Environmental Adaptations for the Elemental and Garden they protect, such as one being out in an area that is snowy most of the year having the Adaptation of the Tundra. Then you have Universal Adaptations that any Nagual can learn, such as Adaptation of the Urban Predator, or the Territory. Finally, there are Supernatural Adaptations, such as Adaptation of Death which you can learn by hanging out with Sin-Eaters too long, or fighting Vampires too much.<br /> <br /> That's...pretty much the core stuff to it.<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> There is a Server dedicated to it. And I have posted about it here before, however, I felt that it wasn't a very good post. It didn't cover what I needed to and it has been a while.<br /> I am currently working on a Night Horrors Supplement for it. The Core Rulebook is finished (though a bit rough as far as editing goes).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rYxBILf2PLVVKgF07shwMY6z9_lIcUEEEfne7iiTV44/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a> (Core-Rulebook)<br /> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/Mzx583YSk\" target=\"_blank\">https://discord.gg/Mzx583YSk</a> (Server)<br /> <br /> <b><i>Themes: </i></b><br /> <br /> <i>Duty: </i>All Nagual are tied by the Rage to Lurra-Ulaka. All of them have a duty and responsibility to use their Rage to protect their Wild Cousins and Lurra's Garden from the Invasives. To turn your back on that duty is to go Wayward.<br /> <br /> <i>Family: </i>Nagual are not only the animals they take the shape of. Even the most independent of them need others to turn to for support and comfort when things get hard. Either their real blood family, or those they choose. Family reminds the Nagual why they fight.<br /> <br /> <i>Community: </i>No Nagual is an island. Gathering in Clans of several members, along with their families and Cinder relatives. The community is the heart of the territory, even the extended human settlements they border or hide among are deeply important to the Nagual. Without a community, the Nagual could turn savage.<br /> <br /> <b><b>Misunderstandings and Fallacies</b></b><br /> <br /> <i><b>All Nagual are part animal</b></i><br /> <br /> <i>Partially. Our lizard brain is certainly a bit more active than that of humans. We begin to take on animalistic traits and urges as our Rage rises beyond our control. We can all turn into various levels of an animal, from full beast to a pure hybrid. But completely part animal to the point of being able to reproduce with them? No, that\u2019s not something we\u2019re capable of. They\u2019re our wild cousins, not our wild spouses. Even those born of animals are forever cut off from them in that way. Mother Lurra wants us to stay with one another and humanity, and so that is who we can *ahem* be with.</i><br /> <br /> <i><b>Being bitten by a Nagual turns you into one.</b></i><br /> <br /> <i>Partially. If we bite you, we intend to kill you, not make you one of us. Though, sometimes accidents do happen. Ingesting or injecting our blood into your veins can result in a new Nagual. However, those that we attack with our claws and teeth do not survive first contact. Certainly, not long enough for the Mother to call them. Even if they are so lucky, they must survive the burn of the Rage, and not lose their minds doing so. A tall order for even ones we select to Kindle.</i><br /> <br /> <i><b>All Nagual are Cursed.</b></i><br /> <br /> <i>Not all of us. Curse is not a word we would use to describe the Rage, though it certainly can be a burden. The Kindled make up enough of us that there are myths and legends associated with lycanthropes. However, they are not the typical Nagual. Most of us are born and raised as Cinders, or Nagual that have not undergone The Call. The barest embers of Rage flow through their veins, and they have small quirks based off of their animal natures that mark them as the other. Others are born and raised as animals before Lurra-Ulaka Calls to them.</i><br /> <br /> <b><i>Nagual Defend Nature from Humans</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>No. Humans are every bit a part of Lurra\u2019s Garden as our Wild Cousins. We are to guide them on how to nurture the Garden, and they are to remember that they are of nature as well. Humanity are the Gardeners, and it is in their hands to see nature flourish. To make an enemy of Humanity is to move one step closer to becoming a Man-Eater or Lycanthrope-to fall Wayward. In the face of the Absence, we are all Lurra\u2019s Children.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27726-tonkers77","user":"Tonkers77","date":". 07-28-2023, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27726-tonkers77","name":"Tonkers77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27726_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T16:36:43-07:00","id":1518967,"title":"","content":"I <i>proooooooobably</i> wouldn't name it Nagual if you're just going for a kind of shapeshifter, given that Nahual is a specific cultural idea that is often abused by the people outside of that cultural background, in the same way it's kind of galling to use the word Wendigo for anything outside it's specific meaning.<br /> <br /> Not the least of which that the Nahual are more likes witches than simple shapeshifters, even with their ability to change shapes as a prominent feature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T18:16:24-07:00","id":1518977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1518965-nagual-the-savage?p=1518967#post1518967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I <i>proooooooobably</i> wouldn't name it Nagual if you're just going for a kind of shapeshifter, given that Nahual is a specific cultural idea that is often abused by the people outside of that cultural background, in the same way it's kind of galling to use the word Wendigo for anything outside it's specific meaning.<br /> <br /> Not the least of which that the Nahual are more likes witches than simple shapeshifters, even with their ability to change shapes as a prominent feature.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm friends with folks from the region in which Nahual is used. They were fine with it.<br /> I do appreciate the concern, and if anyone from the culture is upset then I would be willing to consider a change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27726-tonkers77","name":"Tonkers77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27726_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T19:40:39-07:00","id":1518982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tonkers77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1518965-nagual-the-savage?p=1518977#post1518977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm friends with folks from the region in which Nahual is used. They were fine with it.<br /> I do appreciate the concern, and if anyone from the culture is upset then I would be willing to consider a change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh huh.<br /> <br /> Putting aside the cultural angle and the value of &quot;My [Mexican] friend said&quot; as a defense* regarding the name, the other major catch I have from the brief scan is that you seem at odds with yourself in terms of how much you want people to read it in association with Werewolf or not-and that's cutting both ways with Forsaken and Apocalypse. For starting off the post with &quot;There's no association with the Shadow, so you can play them along with the Uratha&quot;, you have a lot of elements that don't particularly make any sense <i>unless</i> you wanted it to be Forsaken adjacent, except I also get a sense you're not hyper-comfortable with with Forsaken as a language.<br /> <br /> There's a couple of ways you can deal with that, but in the interest of keeping the it simple for ease of excellence, I personally would either tell you to lean into (or more technically accurate, <i>past</i>) the Forsaken-isms, or lean away from it.<br /> <br /> The latter's probably easier, since you can excise a lot of words and even expectations (like Rage) out of your work and get wilder with the mystery behind the splat[s](particularly since you don't have to have a single unified origin for them***) and more directly in theme with a non-Werewolf rooted shapeshifter splat-for a tonal guide, I would point you at anything on the Gangrel from Requiem and towards Hunter First Edition**, both hit the particular voice of a non-spiritual take on the visceral thrill of an animalistic shapeshifter splat.<br /> <br /> THe former is challenging if you don't feel hyper comfortable with the ins and outs of the Forsaken universe, but one particular gem of a feature that you can take root in is the extreme ass end of things with Pangaeans, ancient entities that have explicit roles as being a viable origin for other shapeshifters and often have agendas that can (and, in fact, do) still execute into the modern day, and of course gives you tools to make shifters that also have more uniqueness to them than the usual stuff for shapeshifters. It also gives you plenty of leeway to beg, steal, and borrow from Mage: the Awakening and Beast: the Primordial. The biggest catch is that, while you can anchor things in the triage of the Flesh, Shadow, and Astral (or weirder still, the Sundering that ultimately fucked over the Pangaeans did have far reaching consequences and threw things far afield), you probably still need to have a good grasp of how these things incarnate and play out to keep it versimilitudinous with where-ever you anchor things in the Flesh, Shadow, and Astral. At a bare minimum, you'd probably at least want to have a look at how they did their own alternate shifters, most prominently in War Against the Pure.<br /> <br /> In any particular case, either way, you wanna scrub the Apocalypse-isms out, since it immediately stands out as odd in the text but is also not used enough as it's own language to demarcate it as a deliberate recycling to make a unique Chronicles product.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it looks coherent, keep at it.<br /> <br /> *because we could be here forever if we got into whether I believe you or not and how useful it is as an actual defense or not, and I expect we wouldn't get anywhere for all the motions. I imagine we'll collectively be happier if we don't have that conversation.<br /> **admittedly you'd have to cherry pick here, but I don't have a ready way to point at where to pick from HtV 1E, and to be honest even the parts that aren't rooted in the atavistic thrill you'd be looking for is still rooted in a violence that is gritty, predator-and-prey, and viscerally bloody<br /> ***Also you get to avoid looking like Changing Breeds, which is one thing that I would wager is the thing that will get the most in your way currently for drumming up interest in your project, because regardless of how otherwise coherent I think it looks, that was the second thing that immediately stood out to me and readers will hold that against your project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T05:45:25-07:00","id":1519008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Uh huh.<br /> <br /> Putting aside the cultural angle and the value of &quot;My [Mexican] friend said&quot; as a defense* </div> </div> </div>I apologize for that. That isn't a good defense. I am going to share what research I did do around the term and can further explain how I used this research in my writing of Nagual if you would want me to. I really enjoyed reading about Nagualism, and they were excited that I had asked about them at all.<br /> <br /> So, I've read this: &quot;<b>Nagualism: A Study in Native American Folk-lore and History by Daniel G. Brinton&quot; </b>Because in this day and age, if you're going to name a project that you've put years of your life into you need to know it's source!<br /> <br /> Also, to back up them being just shapeshifters vs witches (as in not just witches who turn into animals) there is this Mexican RPG that my friend loves: <a href=\"https://nahualrpg.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://nahualrpg.com</a> from Powered by the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> You've also got Brittanica (which, yeah, might not be the best source, but hey, it's another one) &quot;<b>nagual</b>, also spelled <b>nahual</b>, personal <a href=\"https://www.britannica.com/topic/guardian-spirit\" target=\"_blank\">guardian spirit</a> believed by some Mesoamerican Indians to reside in an <a href=\"https://www.britannica.com/topic/animal-worship\" target=\"_blank\">animal</a>, such as a deer, <a href=\"https://www.britannica.com/animal/jaguar-mammal\" target=\"_blank\">jaguar</a>, or <a href=\"https://www.britannica.com/animal/bird-animal\" target=\"_blank\">bird</a>. In some areas the nagual is the animal into which certain powerful men can transform themselves to do evil; thus, the word <a href=\"https://www.britannica.com/dictionary/derives\" target=\"_blank\">derives</a> from the Nahuatl word <i>nahualli</i> (\u201cdisguise\u201d), applied to the animal forms magically assumed by sorcerers.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the other major catch I have from the brief scan is that you seem at odds with yourself in terms of how much you want people to read it in association with Werewolf or not-and that's cutting both ways with Forsaken and Apocalypse. For starting off the post with &quot;There's no association with the Shadow, so you can play them along with the Uratha&quot;, you have a lot of elements that don't particularly make any sense <i>unless</i> you wanted it to be Forsaken adjacent, except I also get a sense you're not hyper-comfortable with with Forsaken as a language.<br /> <br /> There's a couple of ways you can deal with that, but in the interest of keeping the it simple for ease of excellence, I personally would either tell you to lean into (or more technically accurate, <i>past</i>) the Forsaken-isms, or lean away from it.<br /> <br /> The latter's probably easier, since you can excise a lot of words and even expectations (like Rage) out of your work and get wilder with the mystery behind the splat[s](particularly since you don't have to have a single unified origin for them***) and more directly in theme with a non-Werewolf rooted shapeshifter splat-for a tonal guide, I would point you at anything on the Gangrel from Requiem and towards Hunter First Edition**, both hit the particular voice of a non-spiritual take on the visceral thrill of an animalistic shapeshifter splat.<br /> <br /> THe former is challenging if you don't feel hyper comfortable with the ins and outs of the Forsaken universe, but one particular gem of a feature that you can take root in is the extreme ass end of things with Pangaeans, ancient entities that have explicit roles as being a viable origin for other shapeshifters and often have agendas that can (and, in fact, do) still execute into the modern day, and of course gives you tools to make shifters that also have more uniqueness to them than the usual stuff for shapeshifters. It also gives you plenty of leeway to beg, steal, and borrow from Mage: the Awakening and Beast: the Primordial. The biggest catch is that, while you can anchor things in the triage of the Flesh, Shadow, and Astral (or weirder still, the Sundering that ultimately fucked over the Pangaeans did have far reaching consequences and threw things far afield), you probably still need to have a good grasp of how these things incarnate and play out to keep it versimilitudinous with where-ever you anchor things in the Flesh, Shadow, and Astral. At a bare minimum, you'd probably at least want to have a look at how they did their own alternate shifters, most prominently in War Against the Pure.<br /> <br /> In any particular case, either way, you wanna scrub the Apocalypse-isms out, since it immediately stands out as odd in the text but is also not used enough as it's own language to demarcate it as a deliberate recycling to make a unique Chronicles product.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it looks coherent, keep at it. </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Thank you very, very much for taking your time on this. I'm not trying to fight you or offend anyone. I really, really just didn't have time to talk yesterday past posting it to the Forums.<br /> <br /> May I ask what you mean by Forsaken-isms? I know it reads a hell of a lot like Apocalypse, which would make sense. This splat began as a Port of the Fera from Apocalypse to CofD. However, it resembling Forsaken is a new thing to me. (Honestly, flattered. I love Forsaken, and heavily analyzed and read that books writing and tones to try and do my best to even come close to it's excellence!) I will read more into the Gangrel and Hunter, though may I ask what part of Hunter would be best?<br /> <br /> During its time in write-up, I had them associated with Pangaeans! Descended from them in the same way that the Uratha and dare I say, Shartha, are. Each of the Broods had a Pangaean progenitor and associated with spirits and such that resembled them. Did you take a look at the document itself, out of curiosity. I would understand if you just don't have time to do that.<br /> <br /> I would like to talk to you further on this project if you don't mind. I honestly really appreciate you taking the time to look at it. I did not mean to come across as dismissive in my earlier post.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27726-tonkers77","name":"Tonkers77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27726_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T06:10:04-07:00","id":1519011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1518965-nagual-the-savage?p=1518982#post1518982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh huh.<br /> <br /> Putting aside the cultural angle and the value of &quot;My [Mexican] friend said&quot; as a defense* regarding the name,</div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize for that. That isn't a good defense. I am going to share what research I did do around the term and can further explain how I used this research in my writing of Nagual if you would want me to. I really enjoyed reading about Nagualism, and they were excited that I had asked about them at all.<br /> <br /> So, I've read this: &quot;Nagualism: A Study in Native American Folk-lore and History by Daniel G. Brinton*&quot; Because in this day and age, if you're going to name a project that you've put years of your life into you need to know it's source!<br /> <br /> Also, to back up them being just shapeshifters vs witches (as in not just witches who turn into animals) there is this Mexican RPG that my friend loves: <a href=\"https://nahualrpg.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://nahualrpg.com</a> from Powered by the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> You've also got Brittanica (which, yeah, might not be the best source, but hey, it's another one) &quot;nagual, also spelled nahual, personal <a href=\"https://www.britannica.com/topic/guardian-spirit\" target=\"_blank\">guardian spirit</a> believed by some Mesoamerican Indians to reside in an <a href=\"https://www.britannica.com/topic/animal-worship\" target=\"_blank\">animal</a>, such as a deer, <a href=\"https://www.britannica.com/animal/jaguar-mammal\" target=\"_blank\">jaguar</a>, or <a href=\"https://www.britannica.com/animal/bird-animal\" target=\"_blank\">bird</a>. In some areas the nagual is the animal into which certain powerful men can transform themselves to do evil; thus, the word <a href=\"https://www.britannica.com/dictionary/derives\" target=\"_blank\">derives</a> from the Nahuatl word nahualli (\u201cdisguise\u201d), applied to the animal forms magically assumed by sorcerers.&quot;<br /> <br /> (I'm writing this again because the bot flagged my former post as Spam! If it gets unblocked and you see this stuff twice I apologize!)<br /> *As it turns out, this guy was a terrible, terrible racist.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27726-tonkers77","user":"Tonkers77","date":". 07-28-2023, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27726-tonkers77","name":"Tonkers77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27726_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T06:12:47-07:00","id":1519012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1518965-nagual-the-savage?p=1518982#post1518982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the other major catch I have from the brief scan is that you seem at odds with yourself in terms of how much you want people to read it in association with Werewolf or not-and that's cutting both ways with Forsaken and Apocalypse. For starting off the post with &quot;There's no association with the Shadow, so you can play them along with the Uratha&quot;, you have a lot of elements that don't particularly make any sense <i>unless</i> you wanted it to be Forsaken adjacent, except I also get a sense you're not hyper-comfortable with with Forsaken as a language.<br /> <br /> There's a couple of ways you can deal with that, but in the interest of keeping the it simple for ease of excellence, I personally would either tell you to lean into (or more technically accurate, <i>past</i>) the Forsaken-isms, or lean away from it.<br /> <br /> The latter's probably easier, since you can excise a lot of words and even expectations (like Rage) out of your work and get wilder with the mystery behind the splat[s](particularly since you don't have to have a single unified origin for them***) and more directly in theme with a non-Werewolf rooted shapeshifter splat-for a tonal guide, I would point you at anything on the Gangrel from Requiem and towards Hunter First Edition**, both hit the particular voice of a non-spiritual take on the visceral thrill of an animalistic shapeshifter splat.<br /> <br /> THe former is challenging if you don't feel hyper comfortable with the ins and outs of the Forsaken universe, but one particular gem of a feature that you can take root in is the extreme ass end of things with Pangaeans, ancient entities that have explicit roles as being a viable origin for other shapeshifters and often have agendas that can (and, in fact, do) still execute into the modern day, and of course gives you tools to make shifters that also have more uniqueness to them than the usual stuff for shapeshifters. It also gives you plenty of leeway to beg, steal, and borrow from Mage: the Awakening and Beast: the Primordial. The biggest catch is that, while you can anchor things in the triage of the Flesh, Shadow, and Astral (or weirder still, the Sundering that ultimately fucked over the Pangaeans did have far reaching consequences and threw things far afield), you probably still need to have a good grasp of how these things incarnate and play out to keep it versimilitudinous with where-ever you anchor things in the Flesh, Shadow, and Astral. At a bare minimum, you'd probably at least want to have a look at how they did their own alternate shifters, most prominently in War Against the Pure.<br /> <br /> In any particular case, either way, you wanna scrub the Apocalypse-isms out, since it immediately stands out as odd in the text but is also not used enough as it's own language to demarcate it as a deliberate recycling to make a unique Chronicles product.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it looks coherent, keep at it.<br /> <br /> *because we could be here forever if we got into whether I believe you or not and how useful it is as an actual defense or not, and I expect we wouldn't get anywhere for all the motions. I imagine we'll collectively be happier if we don't have that conversation.<br /> **admittedly you'd have to cherry pick here, but I don't have a ready way to point at where to pick from HtV 1E, and to be honest even the parts that aren't rooted in the atavistic thrill you'd be looking for is still rooted in a violence that is gritty, predator-and-prey, and viscerally bloody<br /> ***Also you get to avoid looking like Changing Breeds, which is one thing that I would wager is the thing that will get the most in your way currently for drumming up interest in your project, because regardless of how otherwise coherent I think it looks, that was the second thing that immediately stood out to me and readers will hold that against your project.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you very, very much for taking your time on this. I'm not trying to fight you or offend anyone. I really, really just didn't have time to talk yesterday past posting it to the Forums.<br /> <br /> May I ask what you mean by Forsaken-isms? I know it reads a hell of a lot like Apocalypse, which would make sense. This splat began as a Port of the Fera from Apocalypse to CofD. However, it resembling Forsaken is a new thing to me. (Honestly, flattered. I love Forsaken, and heavily analyzed and read that books writing and tones to try and do my best to even come close to it's excellence!) I will read more into the Gangrel and Hunter, though may I ask what part of Hunter would be best?<br /> <br /> During its time in write-up, I had them associated with Pangaeans! Descended from them in the same way that the Uratha and dare I say, Shartha, are. Each of the Broods had a Pangaean progenitor and associated with spirits and such that resembled them. Did you take a look at the document itself, out of curiosity. I would understand if you just don't have time to do that.<br /> <br /> I would like to talk to you further on this project if you don't mind. I honestly really appreciate you taking the time to look at it. I did not mean to come across as dismissive in my earlier post. <br /> <br /> In regards to *<br /> I would rather be further educated on the subject than remain ignorant. I would expect you've had some sort of sensitivity training on the matter, and therefore have more weight to bear in explaining why and why not to do things. <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27726-tonkers77","name":"Tonkers77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27726_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T06:37:02-07:00","id":1519017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tonkers77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1518965-nagual-the-savage?p=1519011#post1519011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I apologize for that. That isn't a good defense. I am going to share what research I did do around the term and can further explain how I used this research in my writing of Nagual if you would want me to. I really enjoyed reading about Nagualism, and they were excited that I had asked about them at all.<br /> <br /> So, I've read this: &quot;Nagualism: A Study in Native American Folk-lore and History by Daniel G. Brinton&quot; Because in this day and age, if you're going to name a project that you've put years of your life into you need to know it's source!<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a member of that culture, but I am a Cherokee. If you were incorporating my tribe's beliefs and practices into your writing, I would suggest you talk to actual elders within the tribe (or the tribal government itself), tell them what you're wanting to do and get their opinions of it. If the elders you talk to all believe you're approaching it respectfully I certainly wouldn't have a problem with it. That's going to mean more than you asking your buddies or you reading about it in a research paper written by an old racist white man. If they tell you that your approach is not respectful, reconsider your approach.<br /> <br /> I will say though that &quot;The Savage&quot; would probably immediately disqualify you from being found to be respectful in your approach.<br /> <br /> And yes, the author of your paper was racist so it is probably not the best source from which you should draw. &quot;At his presidential address to the American Association for the Advancement of Science in August 1895, Brinton advocated theories of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scientific_racism\" target=\"_blank\">scientific racism</a>that were pervasive at that time. As <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Charles_A._Lofgren&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" target=\"_blank\">Charles A. Lofgren</a> notes in his book, <i>The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plessy_v._Ferguson\" target=\"_blank\">Plessy Case</a>,</i> although Brinton &quot;accepted the 'psychical unity' throughout the human species,&quot; he claimed &quot;all races were 'not equally endowed,' which disqualified [some of] them from the atmosphere of modern enlightenment.&quot; He asserted some have &quot;...an inborn tendency, constitutionally recreant to the codes of civilization, and therefore technically criminal.&quot; Further, he said the characteristics of &quot;races, nations, tribes...supply the only sure foundations for legislation, not <i>a priori</i> notions of the rights of man.&quot;<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daniel_Garrison_Brinton#cite_note-2\" target=\"_blank\">[2]</a></sup>\u200b&quot; <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daniel_Garrison_Brinton\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daniel_Garrison_Brinton</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":". 07-28-2023, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T07:01:26-07:00","id":1519023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1518965-nagual-the-savage?p=1519017#post1519017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not a member of that culture, but I am a Cherokee. If you were incorporating my tribe's beliefs and practices into your writing, I would suggest you talk to actual elders within the tribe (or the tribal government itself), tell them what you're wanting to do and get their opinions of it. If the elders you talk to all believe you're approaching it respectfully I certainly wouldn't have a problem with it. That's going to mean more than you asking your buddies or you reading about it in a research paper written by an old racist white man. If they tell you that your approach is not respectful, reconsider your approach.<br /> <br /> I will say though that &quot;The Savage&quot; would probably immediately disqualify you from being found to be respectful in your approach.<br /> <br /> And yes, the author of your paper was racist so it is probably not the best source from which you should draw. &quot;At his presidential address to the American Association for the Advancement of Science in August 1895, Brinton advocated theories of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Scientific_racism\" target=\"_blank\">scientific racism</a>that were pervasive at that time. As <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Charles_A._Lofgren&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" target=\"_blank\">Charles A. Lofgren</a> notes in his book, <i>The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plessy_v._Ferguson\" target=\"_blank\">Plessy Case</a>,</i> although Brinton &quot;accepted the 'psychical unity' throughout the human species,&quot; he claimed &quot;all races were 'not equally endowed,' which disqualified [some of] them from the atmosphere of modern enlightenment.&quot; He asserted some have &quot;...an inborn tendency, constitutionally recreant to the codes of civilization, and therefore technically criminal.&quot; Further, he said the characteristics of &quot;races, nations, tribes...supply the only sure foundations for legislation, not <i>a priori</i> notions of the rights of man.&quot;<sup><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daniel_Garrison_Brinton#cite_note-2\" target=\"_blank\">[2]</a></sup>\u200b&quot; <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daniel_Garrison_Brinton\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daniel_Garrison_Brinton</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, that writer was terrible. I profusely apologize for even citing his work now. I guess my research didn't go in the right directions at times.<br /> <br /> I really did try to approach this with respect. If the name Nagual: The Savage needs to be changed, then that's it. It can be. I'm just not certain that my actual depiction of them is racist. I've put several years of work, and money, into this project. So, It's costly to change something as large as the name itself when it's on commissions I paid for. I'll get together with the server and bounce ideas, see if there's something better that can be done.<br /> <br /> Aside from the name, what did you think of the Splat as a whole? Was there more that needs to be changed about it, or is it just the name? I am, truly, trying to understand and adjust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27726-tonkers77","name":"Tonkers77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27726_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T07:03:04-07:00","id":1519024,"title":"","content":"I'm making a separate post to address the document itself. I'm not doing a super thorough look through, just looking to get a feel for what you've got going on mechanically. <br /> <br /> Your balance may work internally, I'm not sure, but you've definitely gone to the high side of CofD. There's good reasons the Forsaken don't gain more than 3 to any attribute, you giving out +6s to attributes (and your optional rule to use spirit attributes instead of traditional ones) make your product significantly stronger than the other game lines. Then you top it off by giving your race one of the best abilities combat abilities of vampires on and super easy access to aggravated damage. Basically your product is unusable along side anything except maybe Mage. Is that what you want? If not you need to significantly reduce what your splat can do. If you shoot for a power level slightly below the Forsaken, you will be in a much better place. <br /> <br /> I appreciate the fluff of the race having a higher than normal body temperature, but calling that a weakness? Really? And your banes, I appreciate you wanting to tap into the &quot;metals of different worlds&quot; but you've made the banes laughable as banes with the requirements you've put on them. Again, you've made your race far too powerful to be used with other supplements. <br /> <br /> So what was your intent for this game? Is it meant to be played in a world with the Forsaken, the Lost, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T07:06:19-07:00","id":1519025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tonkers77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1518965-nagual-the-savage?p=1519023#post1519023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really did try to approach this with respect. If the name Nagual: The Savage needs to be changed, then that's it. It can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a member of that culture, I can't speak for them. I will say that &quot;savage&quot; has never been used to describe the members of my tribe in a flattering way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T07:32:59-07:00","id":1519027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1518965-nagual-the-savage?p=1519024#post1519024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm making a separate post to address the document itself. I'm not doing a super thorough look through, just looking to get a feel for what you've got going on mechanically.<br /> <br /> Your balance may work internally, I'm not sure, but you've definitely gone to the high side of CofD. There's good reasons the Forsaken don't gain more than 3 to any attribute, you giving out +6s to attributes (and your optional rule to use spirit attributes instead of traditional ones) make your product significantly stronger than the other game lines. Then you top it off by giving your race one of the best abilities combat abilities of vampires on and super easy access to aggravated damage. Basically your product is unusable along side anything except maybe Mage. Is that what you want? If not you need to significantly reduce what your splat can do. If you shoot for a power level slightly below the Forsaken, you will be in a much better place.<br /> <br /> I appreciate the fluff of the race having a higher than normal body temperature, but calling that a weakness? Really? And your banes, I appreciate you wanting to tap into the &quot;metals of different worlds&quot; but you've made the banes laughable as banes with the requirements you've put on them. Again, you've made your race far too powerful to be used with other supplements.<br /> <br /> So what was your intent for this game? Is it meant to be played in a world with the Forsaken, the Lost, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll nix the optional rule and also the Bruin gains +5. Which is high, but it's a bear. What would you suggest to make the animals distinct in their Attribute adjustment for the forms for the larger animals?<br /> <br /> Alright, these are mechanical changes that I can consider. I'm having a kind of development meeting soon with my Server to discuss Nagual. So, this is certainly something that can be brought up. Uratha also can choose to deal aggravated damage to their target by eating them, however I know that this is a Breaking Point against Harmony to do so. So, a hindrance of some sort for choosing to use Rage to deal Aggravated would be suitable.<br /> <br /> Forsaken aren't notably weaker than Mages. Especially in terms of dice pools and the abilities of a pack.<br /> <br /> The higher than normal body temperatures, especially for as high as they go, can make them easy to notice. Which I put down as a definite disadvantage. How are they laughable as banes? Is it that it requires humans to use them as banes? Which is all hunters, as well as Mages and Sin-Eaters, and anything else that says they're human. But, alright. I can change that to whoever wields them. That is 10 banes vs 1-2 that most Splats have.<br /> <br /> It was intended to be played on its own or with crossover. I feel that you are being very aggressive in the delivery of your critique, but it is appreciated all the same.<br /> <br /> (Edit to add, my mind went directly to the bears, when you were actually talking about the Grimalkin and Gumo! Yes, +6 is a lot.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27726,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27726-tonkers77","user":"Tonkers77","date":". 07-28-2023, 10:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27726-tonkers77","name":"Tonkers77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27726_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T07:34:13-07:00","id":1519028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1518965-nagual-the-savage?p=1519025#post1519025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not a member of that culture, I can't speak for them. I will say that &quot;savage&quot; has never been used to describe the members of my tribe in a flattering way.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I do agree with. I'm willing to change that part 100%. Also will be discussed and different ideas will hopefully be tossed around to replace it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27726-tonkers77","name":"Tonkers77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27726_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T08:50:25-07:00","id":1519032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tonkers77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1518965-nagual-the-savage?p=1519027#post1519027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alright, these are mechanical changes that I can consider. I'm having a kind of development meeting soon with my Server to discuss Nagual. So, this is certainly something that can be brought up. Uratha also can choose to deal aggravated damage to their target by eating them, however I know that this is a Breaking Point against Harmony to do so. So, a hindrance of some sort for choosing to use Rage to deal Aggravated would be suitable.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can do aggravated to humans and wolves by eating them. They can also do it to other Uratha. There's no evidence that it applies to any other beings. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Forsaken aren't notably weaker than Mages. Especially in terms of dice pools and the abilities of a pack. </div> </div> </div>This is kind of a tangent, but I think you will find that the majority of players do not agree with you. The general power rankings tend to be Mages and Mummies at the top tier, demons somewhere below them, then Forsaken, vampires, changelings, and prometheans with some variability in where those 4 exactly line up, then sin eaters and hunters. It's not just about dice pools, which is where the Forsaken excel, it's about Mages being able to do things that the Forsaken will never be able to accomplish. That's why I said Mages could be played along side your splat, no matter how OP your splat is, Mages can do anything. <br /> <br /> Forsaken are a good comparison point though for your race, they're at a good point on the power curve for splats and they're doing similar things, they're both combat focused with natural weapons and significant dice pools, they both have good defensive abilities. My suggestion is this, go through the Forsaken book and look at everything they get and make a list. Do the same for yours. See which side is ahead at the end of it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The higher than normal body temperatures, especially for as high as they go, can make them easy to notice. Which I put down as a definite disadvantage. How are they laughable as banes? Is it that it requires humans to use them as banes? Which is all hunters, as well as Mages and Sin-Eaters, and anything else that says they're human. But, alright. I can change that to whoever wields them. That is 10 banes vs 1-2 that most Splats have. </div> </div> </div>Imagine if silver was only a bane to the Uratha in the hands of a six fingered man, standing on one leg, while petting a puppy with his other hand. Would you say that's the same level of a bane as it is currently? It's not even close to the same thing because I added those 3 conditions, right? Your banes also have 3 conditions that have to be fulfilled, the material, the blessing, the human. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It was intended to be played on its own or with crossover. I feel that you are being very aggressive in the delivery of your critique, but it is appreciated all the same. </div> </div> </div>It's a matter of emphasis, there's a lot of work that needs to be done here to bring it into alignment with other games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Edit to add, my mind went directly to the bears, when you were actually talking about the Grimalkin and Gumo! Yes, +6 is a lot.) </div> </div> </div>Bears were the first ones I noticed, but they weren't the worst offenders. <br /> <br /> Now I've only touched on this stuff because I haven't went through the whole document. My best guess would be the merits and any other powers I haven't seen also need revision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}